WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.400
Our seventeenth winter has arrived.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.780
It's not as if anything 
has changed, though.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.650
Who peels the white bits off 
tangerines before eating them?

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.570
Who doesn't?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.020
After all, there's no 
reason to remove them.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.250
I heard that the white 
bits are good for you.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.130
It was on TV yesterday.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.090
Seriously?!

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.450
There's even less reason 
to peel them off now.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.220
I wonder what makes them good for you.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.190
I don't know.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.290
Probably some vitamin or something.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.980
Whatever, just eat them.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.050
But if you eat too many, 
don't your hands turn yellow?

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.440
They do.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.060
Is that bad for you?

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.280
But the herbal medicine, chenpi,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.840
is made from tangerine skins, isn't it?

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:50.730
Chenpi?

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.010
What?

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:53.810
Nothing.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.530
I was just wondering where exactly...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.170
this pointless conversation was going.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.980
You guys must have nothing to do.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.230
Talk about rude!

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.040
You know, we're always <i>very</i> busy, thinking up ways...

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.180
to spend our free time!

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.440
In other words, you've got nothing to do.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.140
Today's tangerines aren't very sweet.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.930
Well, if you squeeze them, 
it makes them sweeter.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.010
This guy's telling us to squeeze them...

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.350
What a pervert.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.220
How do you get that?!

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.980
Such a dirty mind, Kanamecchi.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.210
Look who's talking!

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.000
Instead of staying in the nice, 
warm classroom this winter...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.410
we're out here together, 
for no particular reason.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.140
I'm freezing.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.290
It's your fault for eating 
tangerines out there.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.710
Should we eat in the classroom tomorrow?

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.730
You're bringing tangerines again tomorrow?

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.390
Sorry, but my relatives sent us a ton.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.500
My family can't eat them all ourselves.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.480
Who cares?

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.450
Winter is tangerine season.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.310
Tangerines are good, 
but I want some hotpot, too.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.110
Or udon.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.340
That sounds good.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.680
I'd like to get some hot 
food in me to warm myself up.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.820
Leave the warmth to me.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.660
Is this what you meant by "warmth"?

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.060
Yup. He's nice and warm, isn't he?

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.700
I do feel warm.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.310
Does that feel nice, Master?

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.620
Who are you calling "Master"?

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:46.740
Huh?

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.790
I feel like I've seen something 
similar to this shape before...

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.220
It looks like you two! 
It looks just like you!

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.520
Doesn't it?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.800
This cat certainly is cute 
like Yuta-kun and Yuki-kun.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.540
Not that.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.060
Look at their eyes, and then look 
at the pattern on the cat's back.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:15.620
Besides, in what way are Yutan 
and Yukki cute and cat-like?

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.940
In kindergarten...

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:23.200
They were just like kittens.
 Weren't they just the cutest?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.200
You're asking me if they were cute?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.410
I didn't know Yukki and 
Yutan in kindergarten.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.790
Oh, right.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.520
Let's get a picture.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.370
Yukki, Yutan, stand next to the master.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.000
Come on, hurry up.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.830
Kaname-kun, does your 
mother like tangerines?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.860
I don't think she hates them.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.530
Can we go deliver some 
to her after this?

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.680
She's always taking care of us.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.220
What are you guys doing here?

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.610
And why are you eating?

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.280
More!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.490
Coming right up.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.110
Me, too.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.180
And me, please.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.510
Just a second.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.250
How much are you going to eat?
Show a little restraint when you're a guest.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.290
Thank you for making food for us.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.090
It's fine.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:23.170
Having someone to cook for 
makes it worth cooking.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.170
But, this is seriously good.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.640
I'm sure you'll make a wonderful bride one day.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.640
You're already Dad's wife.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.390
It really is delicious.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.630
I'm so happy to hear that.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:41.900
Kaname-kun never compliments me, 
no matter what I cook for him.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.410
Kanamecchi, you're so cold.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.460
Kaname, that's the sort of 
thing that leads to divorce.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.660
How could it? She's my mom!

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.660
I'm stuffed.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.230
I don't feel like going home anymore.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.470
Kanamecchi, I'm staying here tonight.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.920
What are you babbling about?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.140
Go home.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.670
It's fine.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.720
You don't have school tomorrow.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.660
It's not fine.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.890
Yeah! Why can't I stay over?!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.310
I'll have to look after this 
obnoxious monkey by myself all—

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:14.500
Then, we'll stay, too.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.680
That'll be even more annoying.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.300
Kanamecchi, come on.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.860
No way.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.560
Besides, you guys don't 
have a change of clothes.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.150
I'll go home and get some, then.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:25.950
Ow!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:28.030
If you're going home, just stay there!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.980
All right. We're sleeping over 
at Kanamecchi's place tonight.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.220
I didn't agree to this!

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.440
I need to get my toothbrush.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.620
Let me use your shampoo.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.070
Hey!

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.910
Thank you for letting us stay.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:38.700
Don't mention it.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.040
Okay, Kaname, bye bye for now.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.500
Don't come back!

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.790
The bath's ready for you.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.130
Okay!

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.390
See you guys in a bit.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.890
You're going in first?

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.500
You've got a point.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.060
Kaname-kun, you go first.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.310
What? Let's decide it with 
rock, paper, scissors.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.810
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.400
Shun-chan's such a good kid.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.870
Unlike you, who tried to jump in first.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.910
Hey, guys, does Shun-chan...

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.540
Why are you whispering?

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.040
Just talk normally. It's not like he's in the room.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.200
Oh, right.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.500
Does Shun-chan ever get mad?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.910
Of course he does.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:23.520
I think Shun's actually pretty manly.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.880
He's very headstrong.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.970
Yutan, your answer's too serious.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.810
Wouldn't you get kinda weak in the knees...

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:33.590
if a cute, good-humored kid like him got mad?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.600
That's not at all what we're talking about.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.910
Chizuru, you thought Shun 
was a girl when you first met him.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:44.440
Shun-chan does get angry, but in a 
cute way, with his cheeks all puffed up.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.630
That doesn't count as "angry."

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.750
Right, Master?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.480
Why am I the Master of Anger?

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.910
No one's better at 
getting angry than you.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.330
Whose fault is that?!

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.580
Don't fight, you two.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.670
Yutan, was that...

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.200
I'm Shun.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.640
Shun's usually here to intercede,

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.450
so I decided to try it.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.000
That sounds nothing like him.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.640
Shun-chan's more like this:

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.610
Don't fight, you guys.

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.140
That's not it, Chizuru.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.940
Why can't we all just get along?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:28.240
What? Yuki-kun, that's not right either.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.230
You guys look like 
idiots from over here.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:35.450
Kaname-kun, why don't you 
try joining us some time?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.550
I wanna see Kaname-kun's Shun.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.020
Stop being so weird.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.000
We're serious. You should 
try it, Kaname-kun.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.720
Not a chance.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:48.640
Then, why don't we talk 
about kindergarten?

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.550
We can talk about Kaori-sensei, 
or Kaori-sensei, or maybe even Kaori-sensei.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.410
I wanna hear about it.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.760
You dirty cheats!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.670
That's how badly we want to see you do it.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:02.040
If you understand, just do it already.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.400
Oh, I understand.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.920
I understand just how annoying you all are.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:06.980
Do it, do it.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:10.330
Don't tell anyone.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.980
I'm only gonna do it once.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.440
Okay.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:18.270
Why do you guys always have to fight?

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.470
Can't you try to get along?

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:21.460
Welcome back, Shun.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:24.330
Shun!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.020
Um, no! This isn't what it looks like!

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:31.630
Kaname-kun, I didn't know you 
talked like that sometimes.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.210
Huh?

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:37.360
I'm not saying it's bad or weird...

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.350
I think it's good for people to 
have different sides to them.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.890
What? But, I was...

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.750
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.020
I won.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.930
See you guys later.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.630
Hold on a sec, Yutan.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.520
Yukki, you go with him.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.090
What? Why?

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.900
Yeah, do it.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.020
Can't save us some time?

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:03.150
If we don't get a move on,
 we'll end up getting to bed late.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.040
That's no reason for
 us to go in together.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.520
You're twins, aren't you?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.790
One and the same, right?

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.620
It'll be a two-for-one deal.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:13.040
What are you saying, valedictorian?

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.760
That's not what it means.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.930
Why do you have to force this on us...

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.040
just because we're twins?

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.550
Quit complaining and get going already.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:28.140
I didn't think they'd actually do it.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.690
You're such a child.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.820
Huh? That was fast.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.320
We couldn't relax in there together.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.370
Really?

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.180
Kaname-kun, Chizuru-kun, 
it's one of you two next.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.320
Right, come on.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.790
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.300
Oh, come on!

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.040
I'm last?!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.210
That's karma for your actions today, monkey.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.380
Hey.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.260
Keep an eye on these perverts.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.270
What were you guys doing?

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.880
We were just doing a touch of peeping.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.530
Quit acting like idiots.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:14.650
Do it again and I'll beat you.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.930
I couldn't relax at all.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.200
Go on then, monkey.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:21.820
No.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.820
If I go, I'm sure you 
guys will talk about me...

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.160
behind my back or imitate me.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.250
I don't want that!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.770
It'll be fine, Chizuru-kun.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:35.010
Yeah, don't worry.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.550
There's nothing about you we'd want to talk about.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.300
I don't want that either!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.850
So, which is it?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.300
Quit complaining and get going!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.160
That monkey ruined my quiet night in.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.850
But, isn't this fun?

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:09.050
I feel like Chizuru-kun's 
been with us forever.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:13.870
I always end up talking about 
the past because of it.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.870
I wonder if that bothers him...

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.290
What? I'm sure it's fine.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.660
That was great.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.340
Kanamecchi, your bath is great.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.390
It's so big and clean.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:27.730
Who are you?

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:32.740
All the futons are ready to go.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.650
It's a miracle you could fit 
four futons in one room.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.800
Your room's pretty big, if nothing else.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.610
There's a miracle taking place 
on top of your head right now.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.700
You guys sleep wherever.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.210
Don't let him sleep!

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.000
Don't think I'm going to let 
you slink off to sleep!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.250
We're gonna have lots more fun tonight!

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:56.530
Get up.

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:57.420
Get up.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.380
W-Wait... You guys!

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:04.870
It's true, though.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:07.960
There's nothing to play 
with in Kaname's room.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:08.880
I know.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.730
This room's only suited to 
studying and sleeping.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.840
I can't sleep with you on my bed! Get off!

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.200
Stay up, then.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:18.900
It's always you, isn't it? You little...

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:21.560
Kaname-kun, what about that?

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.110
Don't you have it any more?

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.450
Wow, a telescope!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.440
Kanamecchi, I didn't know 
you had something like this.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.860
I forgot I had it.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:35.830
We all did some stargazing 
back in elementary school.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.400
We stayed over at 
Kaname-kun's house and...

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.050
Wasn't it our summer research project?

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:47.660
Hey, do you think if we look at the moon, 
we'll see those "claimers"?

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.650
You wouldn't be able to see those, 
because they're on Earth.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:54.130
You can see craters, though.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.370
There's a full moon tonight,

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:58.370
so I'm sure you'll be able to see them.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.810
Maybe.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.250
I don't think so.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.730
Even if it's a full moon,

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.080
if Kaname's hogging the telescope,

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:10.140
we won't get to see a single star, 
let alone craters.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.130
You're right.

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:15.790
Why don't you guys try 
becoming stars instead?

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.080
I'll even help you out.

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:18.620
The North Star.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.310
Is that it?

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.090
Dunno. Just guessing.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:23.790
What?

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:26.260
Is it me? Am I the North Star?

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:29.260
Does the world revolve around me?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.270
You might be right.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:35.430
You're always dragging 
everyone around with you.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.530
What do you mean by that?

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.760
I wonder what constellations 
we can see right now.

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:41.560
Orion?

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.060
Isn't that it?

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.650
Look, you can even see Canis 
Major and Canis Minor.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.150
If you connect these three constellations,

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.490
you get the Winter Triangle.

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.500
Yuta-kun and Yuki-kun's 
constellation should be nearby.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:59.000
<b>Gemini</b>

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.500
Look.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.000
You're right.

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:01.720
I heard that there's a myth behind Gemini.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.620
The older brother, Castor, 
was a master horseman.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.170
The younger brother, Pollux, 
was a master boxer.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:11.550
The two brothers got along 
very well together.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.310
But, one day, Castor got involved...

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:17.430
in a petty quarrel and was killed.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.900
The grieving Pollux 
tried to kill himself,

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.150
but because he was 
immortal, he couldn't.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.930
He asked his father, Zeus, to help him,

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:30.030
and he turned them 
both into a constellation,

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.950
so that they could always be together.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.680
Yukki, I know you love your brother,

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.090
but don't do it!

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:43.550
That's the story of Castor and Pollux.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.090
You have to overcome your grief...

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.650
and live for your brother.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:48.950
I'm not too bothered by it,

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:51.720
but could you stop acting like I'm dead?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.920
This myth is just too sad.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.710
The story behind Ursa Major...

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:59.260
is a tragedy of love and hate, too.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:02.850
A nymph falls in love with 
Zeus and bears his child,

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.500
but his angry wife turns the nymph...

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.360
and her son into bears.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.850
The dramas of the night 
sky are so messed up.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.750
People of the past had such 
difficult love lives.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:17.330
I'm sure it's not any 
easier for people today.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:22.620
Like people in love with kindergarten 
teachers much older than them.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.880
Oh, you mean Kaori-sensei? Just kidding.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.880
<i>How long ago was that?</i>

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:30.380
I bet Kanamecchi's still 
into older women.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:33.590
She just happened to be older, too!

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:36.510
He's mad now!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:37.690
It must be true.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.760
You're such a pervert, Kaname-kun.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:40.850
"Too"?

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.850
No, I just...

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:50.580
What are you doing down there, Mom?

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:52.150
Oh, nothing.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.910
You liar. You've been 
eavesdropping on us, haven't you?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.600
N-No, I wasn't.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:59.240
You're all still awake, 
so I came to ask you...

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.910
if you wanted anything to eat.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.220
I didn't come to ask you 
how much of an age gap...

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.300
counts as acceptable for you.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:08.110
So you <i>were</i> eavesdropping!

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:11.730
I'm so sorry. Did we wake you?

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.170
It's fine.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.970
Don't mind me.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.760
Just carry on talking about that last topic.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:19.220
In great detail.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:19.930
Like hell we will!

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:24.210
Come on, Mom. Go back to your room and sleep.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:25.730
But, it's just getting to the good part!

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.730
Hey.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:29.470
I might have a chance.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.440
Just go to bed.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.650
I can't see anything.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.370
Let me look.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.100
We should go to sleep.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:38.950
What?

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.270
Is that the time already?

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:42.650
It sure got late.

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.950
It's cold in here. Close the window.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:47.460
And the curtains.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.070
Leave them open.

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:50.660
Let's look at the stars while we sleep.

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:53.230
I can't sleep if it's too dark.

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:54.970
Fine.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:55.930
I'm turning off the light.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.190
Okay. Good night.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:17:59.710
Good night.

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:03.480
Hey...

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.670
Shut up!

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.590
I'm trying to sleep!

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.140
How long are you gonna keep jabbering on?

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.990
It's not us.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.040
Chizuru's talking and 
laughing by himself.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.610
But Yukki just said you should...

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:24.560
take a <i>lode</i>star off when 
you look at constellations.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.710
What's so funny about that?

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.110
Come on.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:30.270
We're really going to sleep this time.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:41.570
Hey...

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.870
You little...

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.270
I know. This'll be the last time.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.950
Shun-chan, what was everyone like...

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.480
in elementary school?

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:50.950
What were we like?

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.560
No one's really changed.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:57.210
Kaname was class president,

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.880
and Shun was already Shun.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.610
Huh? What does that mean?

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.990
Who was the most popular with the ladies?

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.490
Wasn't it Yuta?

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.580
Yeah, he was.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.690
What? Let's not talk about this.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:12.910
Is it time for a confession, Yuta-sama?

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:16.100
Yuta-kun's always been nice.

00:19:16.100 --> 00:19:17.760
And he could run really fast, too.

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.780
He was fast?

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:23.430
Fast kids get all the girls 
in elementary school.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.110
What about Yukki, then?

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:28.020
He runs fast, too.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:32.290
It's not like Yuki didn't 
have girls chasing him,

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.940
but he's never been all that sociable...

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.570
and he absolutely hates groups.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.320
What a waste.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.830
He's so lucky.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.810
Yutan's always been popular,

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:44.700
and he was the first one 
of us to get a girlfriend.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:48.040
Hey, Yutan, when you were 
dating Takahashi-san,

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.950
did you guys kiss?

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.360
No.

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:53.810
Do we really have to talk about this now?

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:57.760
Come on. You can tell 
us the truth today.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.450
Did you?

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:00.330
I just told you. No.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:02.430
And stop trying to listen in.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:06.280
It wouldn't surprise me if you didn't.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:08.680
You weren't going out for very long.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.690
You guys did break up rather quickly.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.160
Things seemed to be going well, too.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.000
You went to the bookstore 
together and stuff.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.650
I go to the bookstore 
with Yuta all the time.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.070
There's no need to get so jealous.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.490
Even though he complains,

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.960
Yuta always waits for 
me to finish shopping.

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:29.220
He always wakes me up, too.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:33.000
And he's always been nice 
to Shun, not just me.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.470
He's the first to notice 
when someone's in trouble,

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:38.090
and he helps them out.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.590
Yuta's always looking 
out for everyone else.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:45.790
That's because you demand 
his attention every day.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.340
I don't know anything about that.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:49.600
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.560
Stop saying that.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.520
Do you guys remember the time...

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.750
we got first place in 
the school choir contest,

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:59.060
and Watanabe-sensei...

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.810
Yeah, he cried his eyes out.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:02.380
Yeah, I know.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.500
Kaname, you teared up, too.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.200
No, I didn't.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:09.790
Those tears were more beautiful 
than the medal we won.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.130
Shut up.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.830
Do you remember the song we sang?

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:19.450
Oh, I guess you don't know 
who Watanabe-sensei is.

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.060
Huh? It's fine.

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:22.840
It's interesting.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.120
We haven't really talked about...

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:26.840
this sort of thing before.

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.140
You're right.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.310
What? Who was that?

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.480
Sorry.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:42.360
Shun, you should've asked 
for more at dinner.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.860
You guys asked for too much.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:48.250
I'm hungry, too.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.630
Right! Let's go the convenience store.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:51.600
Now?

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:52.730
Let's go.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.120
Even during cold winters,

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.310
I'm sure the rabbit in the 
moon keeps on hopping...

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:04.380
In a moon that quietly illuminates 
even the darkest of nights...

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:08.750
I'm hungry. I'm gonna eat so much.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.820
Me, too.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:11.680
I'm gonna eat a ton.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:14.270
I want hotpot. Or udon.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.240
Hot food would be great right now.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.720
Do you guys want to eat those 
tangerines Shun-chan brought?

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:21.430
You really shouldn't. It's late.

00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:22.780
It'll be fine.

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:25.400
We're gonna stay up all night.

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:42.860
The Rabbit in the Moon Hops All Night Long

00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:19.060
The next episode is "Mary's Christmas."
